* OpenPocket 12AX7 reference -- model B: Norman Koren, "Improved vacuum-tube models for SPICE simulations" (2003),
* 12AX7 parameter set  mu=100  Ex=1.4  Kg1=1060  Kp=600  Kvb=300.  Independent of model A (different equations, different fit).
*   E1 = Vpk/Kp * ln(1+exp(Kp*(1/mu + Vgk/sqrt(Kvb+Vpk^2))))
*   Ip = 2 * E1^Ex / Kg1                 (E1 >= 0, so 1+sgn(E1) = 2 for E1 > 0)
* Grid current is Koren's 3/2-power law above the contact potential:  Ig = Gg * (Vgk+Vct)^1.5  for Vgk > -Vct
* NOT in the 12AX7 set of the paper: Gg and Vct below are ASSUMED (6.2e-4 A/V^1.5, 0.2 V); see report, sensitivity section.
* Interelectrode capacitances (optional, see CPAR): Cgk 2.3p, Cgp 2.4p, Cpk 0.9p (typical 12AX7 data-sheet values).
.subckt tube_koren p g k params: cpar=0
.param Gg=6.2e-4 Vct=0.2
Bg g k I = {Gg}*pwr(max(V(g)-V(k)+{Vct},0),1.5)
Ba p k I = 2*pwr(max(V(p,k)/600*ln(1+exp(min(600*(1/100+V(g,k)/sqrt(300+V(p,k)*V(p,k))),60))),1e-30),1.4)/1060
.if (cpar>0)
Cgk g k 2.3p
Cgp g p 2.4p
Cpk p k 0.9p
.endif
.ends
